{"kind":"grammar","lang":"en","entities":{"n4-903":{"renderings":[{"id":"496d68a9355188c0","role":"label","field":"name","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n4-903"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"Prohibitive"},{"id":"aa2588e0c1b69ddd","role":"prose","field":"shortExplanation","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n4-903"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"A blunt 'do not do this' command."},{"id":"d05b8dfd8e61f7af","role":"prose","field":"longExplanation","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n4-903"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"The prohibitive particle な attaches to the plain dictionary form (never the ます-stem) and is the negative counterpart of the imperative. It is equally blunt."},{"id":"4c2c87730379ea18","role":"prose","field":"formation","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n4-903"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"Verb (dictionary form) + な: 行くな, 食べるな, するな."},{"id":"e4126c73bcea522c","role":"label","field":"derives","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n4-903"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"prohibitive (な / do not)"}]}}}